   "firstResult": "{\"source_created\":\"2016-12-07T00:00:00Z\",\"index\":1,\"medium\":\"1 negative : glass ; 5 x 7 in.\",\"reproduction_number\":\"LC-DIG-anrc-09925 (digital file from original)\",\"links\":{\"item\":\"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2017675689/\",\"resource\":\"https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/2017675689/resource/\"},\"title\":\"Red Cross Baseball Somewhere-in-England. Every big American hospital in England has its baseball diamond or even diamonds, and every afternoon when the weather permits, there is either a scrub game or a real contest with a team from some other hospital or military unit, nearby. The baseball player has one advantage in England, too, the season lasts pretty well into the winter, save for occasional damp days. The photograph shows a part of the baseball grounds at the new Portsmouth base hospital. It is said to be the finest baseball diamond in England\",\"image\":{\"alt\":\"digitized item thumbnail\",\"full\":\"https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/pnp/anrc/09900/09925r.jpg\",\"square\":\"https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/pnp/anrc/09900/09925_75x75px.jpg\",\"thumb\":\"https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/pnp/anrc/09900/09925_150px.jpg\"},\"created\":\"2017-02-28T00:00:00Z\",\"modified\":\"2017-02-28T00:00:00Z\",\"collection\":[\"anrc\",\"diof\",\"minload\",\"pp\"],\"creator\":null,\"call_number\":\"LC-A6196- 55503 [P&P]\",\"medium_brief\":\"1 negative :\",\"source_modified\":\"2017-02-23T00:00:00Z\",\"pk\":\"2017675689\",\"created_published_date\":\"1918.\",\"subjects\":[\"American Red Cross.\",\"England.\",\"Glas"
